@Board info
This screen allows changing board info. Note that the asm file may define
changed names for some of these things in order to describe the meaning for
those flags in that specific world file.

þ Board name: A name for the board, which is displayed in the board list in
the editor, and may also be displayed in game in various ways (although it
never does this automatically).

þ Dimensions: The size of this board. You cannot change the dimensions in
this menu; use the resize menu (ALT+R from the board editor) instead.

þ User data: A unsigned 16-bit integer with no inherent meaning; you can use
it for your own use. (A template may define its use.)

þ Screen: The number of the associated screen. When this board is the active
board during the game, the specified screen is displayed.

þ User flags: No inherent meaning; use them for your own use. (A template
may define the meanings of some of them.)

þ Persist: If selected, then the board's state will be saved when you leave
this board and go to another board, and restored when you come back. If it
is not selected, then the board is reset each time it is entered.

þ Suppress global scripts: If selected, then global scripts are not loaded
on this board. If not selected, it only has an effect if a global script is
defined, and only if stat 1 of this board does not already have a script.
The current state of the global script (including the current instruction,
stack frames, etc) will be retained between any boards that use it.

þ Visible overlay: Makes any visible tiles in the overlay to visible (and
obscuring the board grid), unless suppressed by the screen layout. For a
tile to obscure the board grid, all of the criteria are needed: the tile
in the overlay is marked as visible, the "visible overlay" flag in the
board info is set, the screen layout does not suppress the overlay at that
position, the element of that tile does not suppress the overlay, and the
tile is not within the light area.

þ Always allow saving: Always allows saving the game by the F3 and F5 keys
in the specified circumstances, regardless of the control flags. Normally,
saving is always allowed even if these board flags are not specified, but
when the control flags disable saving, these flags can be used to override
the control flags and allow saving anyways.

þ Exits: Specify the board number of the exit in each direction (0 means
no exit in that direction).

